# local env files
#
# Both plain `.env` and the `.env*.local` variants. `.env` holds the Google web
# client id and the API URL; EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the compiled
# bundle as plain text, so nothing genuinely secret should ever go in them — but
# the file is still per-developer configuration, not something to commit.
# `.env.example` documents the variable names and is committed on purpose.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env*.local

# Firebase config — identifies the project and its API keys
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo

example

# generated native folders
/ios
/android
